Subject: [PATCH] mc: melee steps off an add carrying damage shield

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Majordomo Executus casts Damage Shield (21075) on himself and his adds
every 30 seconds. The `moltencore` strategy never reads the damage shield
aura, so melee keep swinging into a shielded add and take reflected damage.

While an add carries Damage Shield, melee retarget off that add. A new
MajordomoDamageShieldMultiplier returns 0 for melee attacks on a damage
shield add, so the melee bot picks an unshielded target instead.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream adds a damage-shield-aware target check to the Molten Core combat
strategy or the generic melee targeting, at which point this multiplier is
redundant.

APPLIES TO

    mod-playerbots @ 60e6555e4e4b552ee4c6551b466aff648916f38b
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCHelpers.h, MoltenCoreSpells
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCMultipliers.h, MajordomoDamageShieldMultiplier
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCMultipliers.cpp, MajordomoDamageShieldMultiplier::GetValue
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp, RaidMcStrategy::InitMultipliers

Uses only members already present at this pin: `PlayerbotAI::IsMelee`,
`MeleeAction`, `AI_VALUE(Unit*, "current target")`, `Unit::GetEntry`,
`Unit::HasAura`.

